ALVA — Controls Preview and Home Screen UI Update

Objective

Implement two small, polished UI improvements in the Alva game. Both changes must integrate naturally with Alva’s existing design system, component structure, localization, responsiveness, and accessibility.

Tasks:

1. Add the missing directional Mouvement icons to the Joystick preview in Settings → Controls.
2. Add a new, non-functional Download button with a download icon at the bottom-right of the Home Screen.

These are visual/interface changes only. Do not introduce new gameplay mechanics or change existing control behavior.

Project context

Repository: hiyroscript/alva

Alva is a browser-based 2D platform fighting game built with native JavaScript ES modules, HTML, CSS, and Canvas 2D. It does not use a framework or build system.

The UI uses near-black backgrounds, subtle glass-like surfaces, restrained green accents, outlined controls, and original SVG icons.

Before implementing, inspect the relevant source files and understand how the components interact.

Important files:

* js/ui/settings-dialog.js — Settings interface and control previews.
* css/settings.css — Settings layout and preview styling.
* js/screens/home-screen.js — Home Screen construction and navigation.
* css/home.css — Home Screen layout and responsive styling.
* js/ui/icons.js — Shared SVG icon definitions.
* js/localization/strings/en.js — English translations.
* js/localization/strings/fr.js — French translations.
* tests/interface/settings.test.mjs — Settings and Home Screen tests.
* tests/interface/controls-ui.test.mjs — Control icon and input tests.

Respect existing architecture and naming conventions.

