Task 1 — Joystick preview: Add directional icons

Current behavior

Open Settings → Controls.

There are two Mobile Controls options:

* Joystick
* Classic Buttons

Each option contains a miniature preview of its touch-control layout.

The Classic preview correctly displays double-arrow Mouvement icons inside its two smaller circular buttons.

However, the Joystick preview currently displays the two smaller circular buttons without any icons.

The missing icons make the Joystick preview look incomplete compared with Classic.

Required implementation

Update the Joystick preview so that its two smaller circular buttons contain the same Mouvement icons used in Classic.

Specifically:

* The upper-left small circle must contain ICONS.mouvementLeft.
* The upper-right small circle must contain ICONS.mouvementRight.
* The main joystick circle and its inner knob must remain unchanged.

Existing implementation

In js/ui/settings-dialog.js, locate the PREVIEW object.

The Classic preview already uses:

* html: ICONS.mouvementLeft
* html: ICONS.mouvementRight

The Joystick preview currently creates the corresponding .sp-dash--left and .sp-dash--right elements without these icons.

Reuse the existing SVG icons in the Joystick preview, rather than creating replacements.

Visual requirements

The Joystick preview must:

* Display the correct directional double-arrow icons.
* Use the exact same icon design as Classic.
* Center each icon precisely inside its circular button.
* Preserve its existing overall dimensions and layout.
* Maintain equal visual weight between the left and right icons.
* Keep the icons legible on small mobile screens.
* Preserve the selected-card green border treatment.
* Look consistent with Alva’s current dark interface.

The existing CSS selector .settings-preview .sp-dash .icon already defines small icon sizing. Reuse it where possible.

Only adjust CSS if necessary for visual alignment or readability. Avoid unnecessarily changing the size or position of the circles.

Restrictions

Do not modify the actual gameplay joystick, Dash behavior, touch input mappings, saved control configurations, or Classic controls.

This task concerns only the small illustration displayed in Settings.

